# Agentic / implementation routing

Do not infer current project status from historical phase documents, Git history, model memory or tool-specific configuration.

Start from:

- `IMPLEMENTATION.md` — repository implementation entry point;
- `docs/agentic_development_foundation/README.md` — live ADF execution sequence/status;
- `docs/agentic_development_foundation/authority_scope_policy.md` — shared human-directed action/authority policy;
- root `AGENTS.md` — shared repository constitution;
- `docs/implementation/README.md` — sole living implementation-program status authority;
- `docs/implementation/agent_reference_index.md` — compact domain-to-contract/document lookup;
- the active ADF or implementation group plan;
- `docs/concepts/phase_010/09_architecture_consolidation_validation_exit/implementation_handoff.md` — frozen architecture handoff.

**ADF-A is complete. ADF-B and ADF-C are the next eligible Agentic Development Foundation groups.** They may proceed independently/overlap only as allowed by the ADF dependency rules. Implementation 001 follows the implemented Agentic Development Foundation exit.

Human-directed action classes:

- A1 review/inspect/plan: do not edit unless changes are also requested;
- A2 change/build/fix: perform in-scope repository edits, directly necessary supporting tests/status/traceability, and safe validation without repetitive permission prompts;
- A3 external/destructive/scope-expanding: require explicit task-specific human authorization plus repository/team gates;
- A4 architecture/semantic change: follow DMTZ change control.

Rules:

- read only the active group plus domain-specific references needed for the task;
- search stable contract IDs (`REF-###`, `AUTH-###`, `HLTH-###`, `OPS-###`, `EXPL-###`, `INTG-###`, `ARCH-###`) instead of loading whole phases;
- ADF work may add agent configuration, OKF routing, portable workflow/skill sources and deterministic validation helpers;
- product code remains under the active implementation package, not implied by ADF work;
- do not create unrelated follow-on work, delegate repository implementation to other agents, or merge/deploy unattended;
- completing the requested group authorizes reporting the next step, not automatically starting it;
- tool memory and lower-precedence preferences are noncanonical;
- implementation convenience and tool-specific configuration never supersede accepted contracts;
- design-scenario PASS is not executable implementation proof.
